// Phase 6c crash robustness, case 3 (re-attach after FULL population turnover).
// By the time this runs, every process that ever touched the segment is gone —
// one killed violently, one exited normally — so for an interval the segment had
// zero attachers. It still exists and still holds 42.
//
// This is ruling c1 made executable: persistence is SEMANTIC, not an artifact of
// someone holding the segment open. Under an unlink-on-last-detach policy this
// program would fail (it would create a fresh zeroed segment and print 0), which
// is precisely why c1 rejects that policy.
high program(): i32 {
    shared("XSEG_c") let c: i32 = 0
    print(c)
    return 0
}
